[2026-02-04T17:24:33.334Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Research: Amazon Layoffs Total 30,000 Corporate Workers\n\n## Mission\n\nConduct thorough research on this topic and produce a comprehensive report with verified findings, source citations, and confidence assessments.\n\n## Claim to Investigate\n\n> \"Amazon is cutting 30,000 corporate jobs (10% of corporate workforce) while 55% of companies cite AI as a primary driver of 2026 layoffs\"\n\n## Research Question\n\nWhat evidence supports the claim that AI implementation is driving 2026 tech layoffs, and how do current layoff rates compare to previous tech downturns?\n\n## Context\n\nAmazon plans to reduce corporate workforce by 16,000 following 14,000 cuts in October 2025\n\n## Research Approach: Actor Investigation\n\n1. **Profile the actor** - Organization, individual, or entity background\n2. **Track funding sources** - Follow the money, identify stakeholders\n3. **Map relationships** - Connections to other actors, organizations\n4. **Review track record** - Past statements, actions, accuracy\n5. **Identify motivations** - What does this actor gain or lose?\n6. **Check credibility indicators** - Expertise, credentials, conflicts of interest\n\n## Source Bias Note\n\nSource leans center-left - consider seeking center-right perspectives.\n\n## Verification Difficulty\n\nScore: 5/5 - This claim should be relatively straightforward to verify with public data and official sources.\n\n## Original Source\n\nhttps://www.cnn.com/2026/01/31/tech/amazon-layoffs-january-tech-changes\n\n## Required Output\n\nProduce a research report that includes:\n\n1. **Executive Summary** - Key findings in 2-3 sentences\n2. **Verified Facts** - Claims that can be confirmed with high confidence\n3. **Unverified/Disputed** - Claims that cannot be confirmed or are contested\n4. **Key Sources** - Primary sources used with credibility assessment\n5. **Confidence Assessment** - Overall confidence in findings (High/Medium/Low)\n6. **Recommendations** - What additional research would strengthen conclusions\n\n---\n\nBegin research using WebSearch and WebFetch tools. Prioritize primary sources over secondary reporting."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecff7720-544d-482b-91e9-9eb1a0db0dee","uuid":"612dd74e-73ba-4660-92ce-1238377e29a6","isSynthetic":true}
