[2026-02-04T17:25:03.990Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S3SS922RVpV1qd1XoY4Tsv","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"55% companies AI primary driver layoffs 2026 survey statistics\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Resume.org Survey: The Great Turnover: 9 in 10 Companies Plan To Hire in 2026, Yet 6 in 10 Will Have Layoffs\",\"url\":\"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/resumeorg-survey-the-great-turnover-9-in-10-companies-plan-to-hire-in-2026-yet-6-in-10-will-have-layoffs-302654255.html\"},{\"title\":\"2026 tech company layoffs\",\"url\":\"https://www.informationweek.com/it-staffing-careers/2026-tech-company-layoffs\"},{\"title\":\"AI layoffs backfire: 55% of employers admit regret\",\"url\":\"https://hrexecutive.com/the-ai-layoff-trap-why-half-will-be-quietly-rehired/\"},{\"title\":\"Companies Are Laying Off Workers Because of AI’s Potential—Not Its Performance\",\"url\":\"https://hbr.org/2026/01/companies-are-laying-off-workers-because-of-ais-potential-not-its-performance\"},{\"title\":\"6 in 10 Companies Are Planning Layoffs in 2026 Due to Economic Uncertainty, Survey Finds - CPA Practice Advisor\",\"url\":\"https://www.cpapracticeadvisor.com/2025/09/18/6-in-10-companies-are-planning-layoffs-in-2026-due-to-economic-uncertainty-survey-finds/169258/\"},{\"title\":\"AI layoffs or ‘AI-washing’? | TechCrunch\",\"url\":\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/02/01/ai-layoffs-or-ai-washing/\"},{\"title\":\"Resume.org Survey: 6 in 10 Companies Plan To Lay Off Employees in 2026 Amid Economic Uncertainty | The AI Journal\",\"url\":\"https://aijourn.com/resume-org-survey-6-in-10-companies-plan-to-lay-off-employees-in-2026-amid-economic-uncertainty/\"},{\"title\":\"The Layoff Era: Understanding Job Cuts from 2025 to 2026 | by Averageguymedianow | Dec, 2025 | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@averageguymedianow/the-layoff-era-understanding-job-cuts-from-2025-to-2026-e36ab1b62746\"},{\"title\":\"Some companies tie AI to layoffs, but the reality is more complicated\",\"url\":\"https://www.courant.com/2026/02/02/did-ai-really-drive-layoffs/\"},{\"title\":\"Resume.org Survey: 6 in 10 Companies Plan To Lay Off Employees in 2026 Amid Economic Uncertainty\",\"url\":\"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/resumeorg-survey-6-in-10-companies-plan-to-lay-off-employees-in-2026-amid-economic-uncertainty-302559155.html\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here are the key survey statistics on AI and layoffs in 2026:\n\n## Primary Finding About 55% and Economic Uncertainty\n\nEconomic uncertainty is the primary driver cited by 55% of companies planning or conducting layoffs, followed by tariff and trade policy concerns (39%) and AI adoption (35%).\n\n## AI as a Driver of Layoffs\n\nHowever, when looking specifically at AI as the main driver: 55% of 1,000 U.S. hiring managers surveyed by Resume.org said they expect layoffs in 2026, and 44% anticipate that AI will be a top driver of layoffs.\n\n## Additional Context on AI and Job Replacement\n\n28% of companies say they have already replaced jobs with AI, and by the end of 2026, 37% expect to replace roles with AI.\n\n## Important Caveat: AI-Washing\n\nInterestingly, research suggests some companies may be overstating AI's role. 59% of hiring managers admit they emphasize AI when explaining hiring freezes or layoffs because it plays better with stakeholders than citing financial constraints.\n\nThese statistics come from a December 2025 Resume.org survey of 1,000 U.S. business leaders and hiring managers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecff7720-544d-482b-91e9-9eb1a0db0dee","uuid":"dedcc65d-a47c-413f-be09-4b8823f8f103","tool_use_result":{"query":"55% companies AI primary driver layoffs 2026 survey statistics","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01KQY44ZTwzLu86HKc87Df5b","content":[{"title":"Resume.org Survey: The Great Turnover: 9 in 10 Companies Plan To Hire in 2026, Yet 6 in 10 Will Have Layoffs","url":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/resumeorg-survey-the-great-turnover-9-in-10-companies-plan-to-hire-in-2026-yet-6-in-10-will-have-layoffs-302654255.html"},{"title":"2026 tech company layoffs","url":"https://www.informationweek.com/it-staffing-careers/2026-tech-company-layoffs"},{"title":"AI layoffs backfire: 55% of employers admit regret","url":"https://hrexecutive.com/the-ai-layoff-trap-why-half-will-be-quietly-rehired/"},{"title":"Companies Are Laying Off Workers Because of AI’s Potential—Not Its Performance","url":"https://hbr.org/2026/01/companies-are-laying-off-workers-because-of-ais-potential-not-its-performance"},{"title":"6 in 10 Companies Are Planning Layoffs in 2026 Due to Economic Uncertainty, Survey Finds - CPA Practice Advisor","url":"https://www.cpapracticeadvisor.com/2025/09/18/6-in-10-companies-are-planning-layoffs-in-2026-due-to-economic-uncertainty-survey-finds/169258/"},{"title":"AI layoffs or ‘AI-washing’? | TechCrunch","url":"https://techcrunch.com/2026/02/01/ai-layoffs-or-ai-washing/"},{"title":"Resume.org Survey: 6 in 10 Companies Plan To Lay Off Employees in 2026 Amid Economic Uncertainty | The AI Journal","url":"https://aijourn.com/resume-org-survey-6-in-10-companies-plan-to-lay-off-employees-in-2026-amid-economic-uncertainty/"},{"title":"The Layoff Era: Understanding Job Cuts from 2025 to 2026 | by Averageguymedianow | Dec, 2025 | Medium","url":"https://medium.com/@averageguymedianow/the-layoff-era-understanding-job-cuts-from-2025-to-2026-e36ab1b62746"},{"title":"Some companies tie AI to layoffs, but the reality is more complicated","url":"https://www.courant.com/2026/02/02/did-ai-really-drive-layoffs/"},{"title":"Resume.org Survey: 6 in 10 Companies Plan To Lay Off Employees in 2026 Amid Economic Uncertainty","url":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/resumeorg-survey-6-in-10-companies-plan-to-lay-off-employees-in-2026-amid-economic-uncertainty-302559155.html"}]},"Based on the web search results, here are the key survey statistics on AI and layoffs in 2026:\n\n## Primary Finding About 55% and Economic Uncertainty\n\nEconomic uncertainty is the primary driver cited by 55% of companies planning or conducting layoffs, followed by tariff and trade policy concerns (39%) and AI adoption (35%).\n\n## AI as a Driver of Layoffs\n\nHowever, when looking specifically at AI as the main driver: 55% of 1,000 U.S. hiring managers surveyed by Resume.org said they expect layoffs in 2026, and 44% anticipate that AI will be a top driver of layoffs.\n\n## Additional Context on AI and Job Replacement\n\n28% of companies say they have already replaced jobs with AI, and by the end of 2026, 37% expect to replace roles with AI.\n\n## Important Caveat: AI-Washing\n\nInterestingly, research suggests some companies may be overstating AI's role. 59% of hiring managers admit they emphasize AI when explaining hiring freezes or layoffs because it plays better with stakeholders than citing financial constraints.\n\nThese statistics come from a December 2025 Resume.org survey of 1,000 U.S. business leaders and hiring managers."],"durationSeconds":6.036473900000001}}
[2026-02-04T17:25:07.888Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TetTuLNfcDbAZLJLwGkVxx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"tech layoffs 2026 AI implementation workforce reduction statistics\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The AI layoff trap: Why half will be quietly rehired\",\"url\":\"https://hrexecutive.com/the-ai-layoff-trap-why-half-will-be-quietly-rehired/\"},{\"title\":\"2026 tech company layoffs\",\"url\":\"https://www.informationweek.com/it-staffing-careers/2026-tech-company-layoffs\"},{\"title\":\"Layoffs Tracker - All Tech and Startup Layoffs\",\"url\":\"https://www.trueup.io/layoffs\"},{\"title\":\"Companies Are Laying Off Workers Because of AI’s Potential—Not Its Performance\",\"url\":\"https://hbr.org/2026/01/companies-are-laying-off-workers-because-of-ais-potential-not-its-performance\"},{\"title\":\"Are Tech Layoffs Really About AI? The Bigger Forces Reshaping the Tech Workforce\",\"url\":\"https://www.techtimes.com/articles/314229/20260122/are-tech-layoffs-really-about-ai-bigger-forces-reshaping-tech-workforce.htm\"},{\"title\":\"AI layoffs or ‘AI-washing’? | TechCrunch\",\"url\":\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/02/01/ai-layoffs-or-ai-washing/\"},{\"title\":\"New Research Reveals 276,000+ Tech Workers Lost Jobs to AI-Driven Layoffs in 2024-2025\",\"url\":\"https://www.einpresswire.com/article/886940804/new-research-reveals-276-000-tech-workers-lost-jobs-to-ai-driven-layoffs-in-2024-2025\"},{\"title\":\"McKinsey Report Finds 30% of Companies Planning Layoffs Due to AI in 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.finalroundai.com/blog/mckinsey-report-layoffs-due-to-ai\"},{\"title\":\"Tech jobs in 2026: layoffs, AI hype, and new roles - Rest of World\",\"url\":\"https://restofworld.org/2026/tech-jobs-2026-ai-layoffs-hybrid-work/\"},{\"title\":\"Tech Sector Hit by Widespread Layoffs in 2025-2026: AI Reshapes the Workforce\",\"url\":\"https://ekhbary.com/news/tech-sector-hit-by-widespread-layoffs-in-2025-2026-ai-reshapes-the-workforce-660-2.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about tech layoffs in 2026 and AI implementation's impact on workforce reduction:\n\n## 2026 Tech Layoff Statistics\n\nSo far in 2026, there have been 28 layoffs at tech companies with 5,285 people impacted (294 people per day), though nearly 245,000 tech jobs were cut in 2025, with about 70% of those layoffs stemming from U.S.-headquartered companies.\n\nAI was the cause of nearly 55,000 layoffs in the U.S. in 2025, though the picture is more complex in 2026.\n\n## Major 2026 Layoff Announcements\n\nSeveral major tech companies have announced significant reductions:\n- Meta kicked off 2026 layoffs with a reduction of about 1,500 employees from its Reality Labs division\n- Amazon plans to reduce its corporate workforce by 16,000 employees, which comes after reductions in October 2025 led to layoffs of 14,000 corporate employees. Together, the layoffs of 30,000 amount to about 10% of Amazon's corporate workforce\n- ASML plans to lay off 1,700 employees, mainly affecting management roles in the company's IT and tech departments, with the company planning to shift these management positions to more engineering roles\n\n## The AI Implementation Reality\n\nInterestingly, half of AI-attributed layoffs will be quietly rehired, but offshore or at significantly lower salaries, according to Forrester Research. According to Forrester, 55% of employers report regretting laying off workers for AI, however in many instances companies are laying off workers for AI capabilities that don't exist yet, betting on future promises rather than proven technology.\n\nA new McKinsey report reveals that 30% of companies are preparing to cut jobs due to AI, with most not having fully adopted the technology but workforce changes have already begun.\n\n## Beyond AI: Broader Economic Factors\n\nWhile AI is cited frequently, deep analysis shows that restructuring, market pressures, and overstaffing from earlier hiring surges were far bigger drivers of layoffs than AI implementation alone.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecff7720-544d-482b-91e9-9eb1a0db0dee","uuid":"9fd524e3-11ae-462f-a92a-cfc004d0e8ec","tool_use_result":{"query":"tech layoffs 2026 AI implementation workforce reduction statistics","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01KgjnPZiNAHvoUHZd1pRwNC","content":[{"title":"The AI layoff trap: Why half will be quietly rehired","url":"https://hrexecutive.com/the-ai-layoff-trap-why-half-will-be-quietly-rehired/"},{"title":"2026 tech company layoffs","url":"https://www.informationweek.com/it-staffing-careers/2026-tech-company-layoffs"},{"title":"Layoffs Tracker - All Tech and Startup Layoffs","url":"https://www.trueup.io/layoffs"},{"title":"Companies Are Laying Off Workers Because of AI’s Potential—Not Its Performance","url":"https://hbr.org/2026/01/companies-are-laying-off-workers-because-of-ais-potential-not-its-performance"},{"title":"Are Tech Layoffs Really About AI? The Bigger Forces Reshaping the Tech Workforce","url":"https://www.techtimes.com/articles/314229/20260122/are-tech-layoffs-really-about-ai-bigger-forces-reshaping-tech-workforce.htm"},{"title":"AI layoffs or ‘AI-washing’? | TechCrunch","url":"https://techcrunch.com/2026/02/01/ai-layoffs-or-ai-washing/"},{"title":"New Research Reveals 276,000+ Tech Workers Lost Jobs to AI-Driven Layoffs in 2024-2025","url":"https://www.einpresswire.com/article/886940804/new-research-reveals-276-000-tech-workers-lost-jobs-to-ai-driven-layoffs-in-2024-2025"},{"title":"McKinsey Report Finds 30% of Companies Planning Layoffs Due to AI in 2026","url":"https://www.finalroundai.com/blog/mckinsey-report-layoffs-due-to-ai"},{"title":"Tech jobs in 2026: layoffs, AI hype, and new roles - Rest of World","url":"https://restofworld.org/2026/tech-jobs-2026-ai-layoffs-hybrid-work/"},{"title":"Tech Sector Hit by Widespread Layoffs in 2025-2026: AI Reshapes the Workforce","url":"https://ekhbary.com/news/tech-sector-hit-by-widespread-layoffs-in-2025-2026-ai-reshapes-the-workforce-660-2.html"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about tech layoffs in 2026 and AI implementation's impact on workforce reduction:\n\n## 2026 Tech Layoff Statistics\n\nSo far in 2026, there have been 28 layoffs at tech companies with 5,285 people impacted (294 people per day), though nearly 245,000 tech jobs were cut in 2025, with about 70% of those layoffs stemming from U.S.-headquartered companies.\n\nAI was the cause of nearly 55,000 layoffs in the U.S. in 2025, though the picture is more complex in 2026.\n\n## Major 2026 Layoff Announcements\n\nSeveral major tech companies have announced significant reductions:\n- Meta kicked off 2026 layoffs with a reduction of about 1,500 employees from its Reality Labs division\n- Amazon plans to reduce its corporate workforce by 16,000 employees, which comes after reductions in October 2025 led to layoffs of 14,000 corporate employees. Together, the layoffs of 30,000 amount to about 10% of Amazon's corporate workforce\n- ASML plans to lay off 1,700 employees, mainly affecting management roles in the company's IT and tech departments, with the company planning to shift these management positions to more engineering roles\n\n## The AI Implementation Reality\n\nInterestingly, half of AI-attributed layoffs will be quietly rehired, but offshore or at significantly lower salaries, according to Forrester Research. According to Forrester, 55% of employers report regretting laying off workers for AI, however in many instances companies are laying off workers for AI capabilities that don't exist yet, betting on future promises rather than proven technology.\n\nA new McKinsey report reveals that 30% of companies are preparing to cut jobs due to AI, with most not having fully adopted the technology but workforce changes have already begun.\n\n## Beyond AI: Broader Economic Factors\n\nWhile AI is cited frequently, deep analysis shows that restructuring, market pressures, and overstaffing from earlier hiring surges were far bigger drivers of layoffs than AI implementation alone."],"durationSeconds":9.554778199999998}}
