[2026-02-04T17:25:23.870Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UWdLoxpqwBjA7LNU9XWV7P","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Amazon corporate workforce total employees 2025 2026 percentage layoffs\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Amazon laying off about 16,000 corporate workers in latest anti-bureaucracy push\",\"url\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/01/28/amazon-layoffs-anti-bureaucracy-ai.html\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon's layoffs are staggering. We've seen this before\",\"url\":\"https://www.cnn.com/2026/01/31/tech/amazon-layoffs-january-tech-changes\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon Announced Another Round Of Massive Layoffs\",\"url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/amazon-announced-another-round-massive-233000120.html\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon lays off 16,000 corporate workers in latest round of job losses | CBC News\",\"url\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/news/business/amazon-prematurely-alerts-layoffs-canada-us-9.7064378\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon layoffs hit nearly 2,200 in Washington state, more than half in core product and engineering roles – GeekWire\",\"url\":\"https://www.geekwire.com/2026/amazon-layoffs-hit-nearly-2200-in-washington-state-more-than-half-in-core-product-and-engineering-roles/\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon confirms 16000 more corporate job cuts, bringing ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.geekwire.com/2026/amazon-confirms-16000-more-job-cuts-bringing-total-layoffs-to-30000-since-october/\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon Confirms It’s Slashing 14,000 Jobs, Anticipates More Layoffs In 2026\",\"url\":\"https://deadline.com/2025/10/amazon-slashing-housands-of-corporate-jobs-reuters-report-1236599112/\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon layoffs set to hit Washington corporate workforce hard as AI reliance grows\",\"url\":\"https://komonews.com/news/local/amazon-layoffs-set-to-hit-washington-corporate-workforce-hard-as-ai-reliance-grows-artificial-intelligence-office-fulfilment-center-prime-order-2-day-shipping-seattl-customer-service-downtown-hr-tech-it-economy-jobs\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon Layoffs 2025: What They Mean for the Labor Market and the Future of Work – DAVRON\",\"url\":\"https://www.davron.net/amazon-layoffs-2025-labor-market-impact/\"},{\"title\":\"Aboutamazon\",\"url\":\"https://www.aboutamazon.com/news/company-news/amazon-layoffs-corporate-jan-2026\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Amazon's corporate workforce and layoffs in 2025-2026:\n\n## Recent Layoffs\n\nIn October 2025, 14,000 employees were laid off across Amazon's corporate workforce, and this was followed by another round in January 2026 affecting 16,000 corporate employees.\n\n## Percentage Impact\n\nThe 30,000 jobs that Amazon has eliminated in the past three months is equivalent to about 9% of its staff. For context, the October layoffs of 14,000 would have represented roughly 10% of the company's 350,000 corporate employees.\n\n## Total Workforce Size\n\nAmazon's total global workforce of some 1.5 million full time and part time is much larger and comprised largely of warehouse employees.\n\n## Future Outlook\n\nThe company indicated the cuts would continue in 2026 as it found \"additional places we can remove layers\". Amazon CEO Andy Jassy's goal is to get more done with artificial intelligence — instead of people, with the expectation that this will reduce the total corporate workforce in the next few years as the company gets efficiency gains from using AI extensively.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecff7720-544d-482b-91e9-9eb1a0db0dee","uuid":"f2287506-7431-414c-9855-a662ae8f004e","tool_use_result":{"query":"Amazon corporate workforce total employees 2025 2026 percentage layoffs","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_0141UHJKtxf85JmhDnNfaMVJ","content":[{"title":"Amazon laying off about 16,000 corporate workers in latest anti-bureaucracy push","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/01/28/amazon-layoffs-anti-bureaucracy-ai.html"},{"title":"Amazon's layoffs are staggering. We've seen this before","url":"https://www.cnn.com/2026/01/31/tech/amazon-layoffs-january-tech-changes"},{"title":"Amazon Announced Another Round Of Massive Layoffs","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/amazon-announced-another-round-massive-233000120.html"},{"title":"Amazon lays off 16,000 corporate workers in latest round of job losses | CBC News","url":"https://www.cbc.ca/news/business/amazon-prematurely-alerts-layoffs-canada-us-9.7064378"},{"title":"Amazon layoffs hit nearly 2,200 in Washington state, more than half in core product and engineering roles – GeekWire","url":"https://www.geekwire.com/2026/amazon-layoffs-hit-nearly-2200-in-washington-state-more-than-half-in-core-product-and-engineering-roles/"},{"title":"Amazon confirms 16000 more corporate job cuts, bringing ...","url":"https://www.geekwire.com/2026/amazon-confirms-16000-more-job-cuts-bringing-total-layoffs-to-30000-since-october/"},{"title":"Amazon Confirms It’s Slashing 14,000 Jobs, Anticipates More Layoffs In 2026","url":"https://deadline.com/2025/10/amazon-slashing-housands-of-corporate-jobs-reuters-report-1236599112/"},{"title":"Amazon layoffs set to hit Washington corporate workforce hard as AI reliance grows","url":"https://komonews.com/news/local/amazon-layoffs-set-to-hit-washington-corporate-workforce-hard-as-ai-reliance-grows-artificial-intelligence-office-fulfilment-center-prime-order-2-day-shipping-seattl-customer-service-downtown-hr-tech-it-economy-jobs"},{"title":"Amazon Layoffs 2025: What They Mean for the Labor Market and the Future of Work – DAVRON","url":"https://www.davron.net/amazon-layoffs-2025-labor-market-impact/"},{"title":"Aboutamazon","url":"https://www.aboutamazon.com/news/company-news/amazon-layoffs-corporate-jan-2026"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about Amazon's corporate workforce and layoffs in 2025-2026:\n\n## Recent Layoffs\n\nIn October 2025, 14,000 employees were laid off across Amazon's corporate workforce, and this was followed by another round in January 2026 affecting 16,000 corporate employees.\n\n## Percentage Impact\n\nThe 30,000 jobs that Amazon has eliminated in the past three months is equivalent to about 9% of its staff. For context, the October layoffs of 14,000 would have represented roughly 10% of the company's 350,000 corporate employees.\n\n## Total Workforce Size\n\nAmazon's total global workforce of some 1.5 million full time and part time is much larger and comprised largely of warehouse employees.\n\n## Future Outlook\n\nThe company indicated the cuts would continue in 2026 as it found \"additional places we can remove layers\". Amazon CEO Andy Jassy's goal is to get more done with artificial intelligence — instead of people, with the expectation that this will reduce the total corporate workforce in the next few years as the company gets efficiency gains from using AI extensively."],"durationSeconds":7.638759299999998}}
[2026-02-04T17:25:23.947Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0193Xrf8SAaoSsfyrFQ8kSeL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"tech layoffs 2022 2023 comparison 2026 dot-com bubble historical\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Tech layoffs have soared to the highest level in more than two decades | Fortune\",\"url\":\"https://fortune.com/2023/06/01/tech-layoffs-worst-since-dot-com-bubble-burst/\"},{\"title\":\"Q1 of 2023: The most Tech Layoffs in history\",\"url\":\"https://lunduke.substack.com/p/q1-of-2023-the-most-tech-layoffs\"},{\"title\":\"Tech layoffs increase more than tenfold from 2021 to 2022 | Fortune\",\"url\":\"https://fortune.com/2023/01/03/tech-layoffs-2022-pandemic-dotcom-bubble/\"},{\"title\":\"Q&A: UW researcher discusses the “cruel optimism” of tech industry layoffs | UW News\",\"url\":\"https://www.washington.edu/news/2025/05/14/tech-industry-layoffs/\"},{\"title\":\"White Paper An Evaluation of the 2022 - 2023 Tech Layoffs\",\"url\":\"https://yellowtail.tech/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/White_Paper.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Tech sector layoffs explained: What you need to know\",\"url\":\"https://www.techtarget.com/whatis/feature/Tech-sector-layoffs-explained-What-you-need-to-know\"},{\"title\":\"2022-2023 layoffs vs dotcom | Tech Industry - Blind\",\"url\":\"https://www.teamblind.com/post/2022-2023-layoffs-vs-dotcom-L8UDbm08\"},{\"title\":\"Tech Layoffs Highest Since Dot-Com Crash - Slashdot\",\"url\":\"https://tech.slashdot.org/story/24/03/15/2340257/tech-layoffs-highest-since-dot-com-crash\"},{\"title\":\"Laid-off tech workers turn to LinkedIn, therapy and one another to bounce back\",\"url\":\"https://www.nbcnews.com/business/economy/tech-workers-layoffs-job-cuts-careers-rcna141735\"},{\"title\":\"Big Tech Layoffs: Has the Bubble Burst?\",\"url\":\"https://impakter.com/big-tech-layoffs-has-the-industrys-bubble-burst/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's a comprehensive comparison of tech layoffs in 2022-2023 with historical context:\n\n## 2022-2023 Tech Layoff Scope\n\nIn 2022, 153,160 tech workers lost their jobs, and this trend accelerated dramatically in 2023. In 2023, more than 260,000 workers across nearly 1,200 tech companies lost their jobs. Between 2022 and 2024, more than 500,000 tech workers were laid off.\n\n## Comparison to the Dot-Com Bubble\n\nThe 2022-2023 layoffs represent the most significant tech industry disruption since the dot-com crash. The May 2023 Challenger Report reveals that the recent trend of job cuts marked the highest in the technology sector since 2001—following the Dot-com bubble. 2023 was the second-biggest year of cuts on record in the technology sector, behind only the dot-com crash in 2001.\n\nHowever, in absolute numbers, the dot-com crash was more severe. The dotcom crash led to over 1 million people getting fired, while there were approximately 215,000 layoffs since 2022, making the current situation about 20% as bad as the dotcom crash so far.\n\n## Key Contributing Factors\n\nSeveral factors contributed to tech layoffs, including the economy, inflation, higher interest rates, overhiring and COVID-19 pandemic job correction. Many firms' CEOs gave a similar reason for the large scale of layoffs: over-hiring during the pandemic as the tech industry rapidly expanded.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecff7720-544d-482b-91e9-9eb1a0db0dee","uuid":"cd942d81-7ca2-4ae9-8128-7e0c9394cb5b","tool_use_result":{"query":"tech layoffs 2022 2023 comparison 2026 dot-com bubble historical","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Dv62QPB6tpkNCN7snPtgeH","content":[{"title":"Tech layoffs have soared to the highest level in more than two decades | Fortune","url":"https://fortune.com/2023/06/01/tech-layoffs-worst-since-dot-com-bubble-burst/"},{"title":"Q1 of 2023: The most Tech Layoffs in history","url":"https://lunduke.substack.com/p/q1-of-2023-the-most-tech-layoffs"},{"title":"Tech layoffs increase more than tenfold from 2021 to 2022 | Fortune","url":"https://fortune.com/2023/01/03/tech-layoffs-2022-pandemic-dotcom-bubble/"},{"title":"Q&A: UW researcher discusses the “cruel optimism” of tech industry layoffs | UW News","url":"https://www.washington.edu/news/2025/05/14/tech-industry-layoffs/"},{"title":"White Paper An Evaluation of the 2022 - 2023 Tech Layoffs","url":"https://yellowtail.tech/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/White_Paper.pdf"},{"title":"Tech sector layoffs explained: What you need to know","url":"https://www.techtarget.com/whatis/feature/Tech-sector-layoffs-explained-What-you-need-to-know"},{"title":"2022-2023 layoffs vs dotcom | Tech Industry - Blind","url":"https://www.teamblind.com/post/2022-2023-layoffs-vs-dotcom-L8UDbm08"},{"title":"Tech Layoffs Highest Since Dot-Com Crash - Slashdot","url":"https://tech.slashdot.org/story/24/03/15/2340257/tech-layoffs-highest-since-dot-com-crash"},{"title":"Laid-off tech workers turn to LinkedIn, therapy and one another to bounce back","url":"https://www.nbcnews.com/business/economy/tech-workers-layoffs-job-cuts-careers-rcna141735"},{"title":"Big Tech Layoffs: Has the Bubble Burst?","url":"https://impakter.com/big-tech-layoffs-has-the-industrys-bubble-burst/"}]},"Based on the search results, here's a comprehensive comparison of tech layoffs in 2022-2023 with historical context:\n\n## 2022-2023 Tech Layoff Scope\n\nIn 2022, 153,160 tech workers lost their jobs, and this trend accelerated dramatically in 2023. In 2023, more than 260,000 workers across nearly 1,200 tech companies lost their jobs. Between 2022 and 2024, more than 500,000 tech workers were laid off.\n\n## Comparison to the Dot-Com Bubble\n\nThe 2022-2023 layoffs represent the most significant tech industry disruption since the dot-com crash. The May 2023 Challenger Report reveals that the recent trend of job cuts marked the highest in the technology sector since 2001—following the Dot-com bubble. 2023 was the second-biggest year of cuts on record in the technology sector, behind only the dot-com crash in 2001.\n\nHowever, in absolute numbers, the dot-com crash was more severe. The dotcom crash led to over 1 million people getting fired, while there were approximately 215,000 layoffs since 2022, making the current situation about 20% as bad as the dotcom crash so far.\n\n## Key Contributing Factors\n\nSeveral factors contributed to tech layoffs, including the economy, inflation, higher interest rates, overhiring and COVID-19 pandemic job correction. Many firms' CEOs gave a similar reason for the large scale of layoffs: over-hiring during the pandemic as the tech industry rapidly expanded."],"durationSeconds":8.225426999999996}}
