[2026-02-04T17:25:36.497Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UNz1NDN3LSojfnBKEY9fke","type":"tool_result","content":"# Amazon Layoff Details - January 2026\n\n## 1) Number of Jobs Cut\nApproximately 16,000 roles across Amazon will be impacted by these organizational changes.\n\n## 2) Timeline of Layoffs\nThe reductions were announced on January 28, 2026. US-based employees receive 90 days to seek internal positions; international timing varies by local requirements. The message indicates some teams completed organizational adjustments in October 2025, while others finalized changes on the announcement date.\n\n## 3) Reasons Given for Layoffs\nAmazon cited organizational strengthening through three mechanisms: \"reducing layers, increasing ownership, and removing bureaucracy.\" The company emphasizes it remains \"in the early stages of building every one of our businesses and there's significant opportunity ahead.\"\n\n## 4) Affected Divisions\nThe announcement provides no specifics about which divisions face cuts, describing them only as \"teams\" across the broader organization.\n\n## 5) Mention of AI\nNo direct reference to artificial intelligence appears in this announcement regarding the layoffs' rationale.\n\n## 6) Executive Statements\n**Beth Galetti, Senior Vice President of People Experience and Technology**, delivered the message. She emphasized this isn't \"the beginning of a new rhythm\" of frequent reductions and stated: \"I'm grateful for how our teams continue to deliver – for customers, for each other, and for the incredible things we're building together.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecff7720-544d-482b-91e9-9eb1a0db0dee","uuid":"c6a021cf-b951-4ae3-984e-1f2c82fcf7c7","tool_use_result":{"bytes":161581,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Amazon Layoff Details - January 2026\n\n## 1) Number of Jobs Cut\nApproximately 16,000 roles across Amazon will be impacted by these organizational changes.\n\n## 2) Timeline of Layoffs\nThe reductions were announced on January 28, 2026. US-based employees receive 90 days to seek internal positions; international timing varies by local requirements. The message indicates some teams completed organizational adjustments in October 2025, while others finalized changes on the announcement date.\n\n## 3) Reasons Given for Layoffs\nAmazon cited organizational strengthening through three mechanisms: \"reducing layers, increasing ownership, and removing bureaucracy.\" The company emphasizes it remains \"in the early stages of building every one of our businesses and there's significant opportunity ahead.\"\n\n## 4) Affected Divisions\nThe announcement provides no specifics about which divisions face cuts, describing them only as \"teams\" across the broader organization.\n\n## 5) Mention of AI\nNo direct reference to artificial intelligence appears in this announcement regarding the layoffs' rationale.\n\n## 6) Executive Statements\n**Beth Galetti, Senior Vice President of People Experience and Technology**, delivered the message. She emphasized this isn't \"the beginning of a new rhythm\" of frequent reductions and stated: \"I'm grateful for how our teams continue to deliver – for customers, for each other, and for the incredible things we're building together.\"","durationMs":6272,"url":"https://www.aboutamazon.com/news/company-news/amazon-layoffs-corporate-jan-2026"}}
